<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 10 June, from 1190 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1190 CE <span class="tih-ago">836 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick Barbarossa drowns on the Third Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> drowned in the Saleph river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> while leading his army to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>. Much of the German crusading force broke up after his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1692 CE <span class="tih-ago">334 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bridget Bishop is hanged in the Salem witch trials</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bridget <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> was the first person executed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials">Salem witch trials</a>. By September eighteen more had been hanged, and one man had been pressed to death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1793 CE <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">National Museum of Natural History is founded in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Convention reorganised the royal botanical garden as the Muséum national d'histoire naturelle. Scientists there, including Lamarck and Cuvier, transformed biology and palaeontology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 CE <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">SS troops massacre the village of Oradour-sur-Glane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> unit killed 643 people in the French village, shooting the men and burning women and children in the church. The ruins are preserved as a memorial.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1967 CE <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Six-Day War ends in a ceasefire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fighting ended with Israel holding Sinai, Gaza, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a>. The status of these territories has remained central to the conflict ever since.</p></div></li></ol>
